## Overview

`__SERVICE_NAME__` is a Python 3.12 FastAPI service backed by SQLAlchemy 2.x (sync) and PostgreSQL (with SQLite supported for local development without Docker).

> **Note:** Database tables are currently created at application startup via `Base.metadata.create_all`. Schema migrations will arrive in a later template version.

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/health` | Liveness probe (`{"status": "ok"}`) |
| `GET` | `/health/ready` | Readiness probe (`SELECT 1` -> `200` or `503`) |
| `POST` | `/items` | Create an item (`name`: 1–100 chars, `quantity`: int >= 0) -> `201` |
| `GET` | `/items` | List all items |
| `GET` | `/items/{id}` | Get an item by ID (`404` if missing) |
| `PATCH` | `/items/{id}` | Update an item (`404` if missing) |
| `DELETE` | `/items/{id}` | Delete an item (`204`, `404` if missing) |

## Run Locally (without Docker)

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -c constraints.txt -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

By default, `DATABASE_URL` falls back to `sqlite:///./app.db` and `SERVICE_NAME` defaults to `__SERVICE_NAME__`.

## Run Tests

```bash
pytest
ruff check app tests
ruff format --check app tests
```

## Run with Docker Compose

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and set a strong POSTGRES_PASSWORD
docker compose up --build
```

